WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:05.548
One by one the short winter days came and went.

2
00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:12.321
But for Pollyanna the days were long and sometimes full of pain.

3
00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:21.456
While other children went skating on the frozen ice or sledding on the snowy hills, Pollyanna lay in bed.

4
00:00:21.457 --> 00:00:27.130
Now that Aunt Polly was playing the Glad Game, Pollyanna tried to be cheerful.

5
00:00:27.131 --> 00:00:32.178
Like Mrs. Snow, Pollyanna had taken up knitting.

6
00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:37.644
"At least I can still use my arms and hands!" she said to Aunt Polly.

7
00:00:37.645 --> 00:00:47.848
"Hold out your arms, and we'll wind this yarn into a ball," Aunt Polly said.

8
00:00:47.849 --> 00:00:51.133
They had just finished when Nancy entered the room.

9
00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:55.118
"You have two visitors, Pollyanna," she said.

10
00:00:55.119 --> 00:01:02.706
"Two at once?" Pollyanna was delighted. "I rarely have one."

11
00:01:02.707 --> 00:01:08.202
"I'd better go see who they are," Aunt Polly said.

12
00:01:08.203 --> 00:01:13.514
A few minutes later, Mr. Pendleton and Jimmy entered Pollyanna's room.

13
00:01:13.515 --> 00:01:19.292
Mr. Pendleton was carrying another prism, and Jimmy had a box of chocolates.

14
00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:23.041
"We won't stay long," Mr. Pendleton said.

15
00:01:23.042 --> 00:01:30.234
"I just wanted you to know how well Jimmy's doing. He's turning into a fine boy!"

16
00:01:30.235 --> 00:01:38.622
"I have a wonderful home now," Jimmy added. "Mr. Pendleton is turning into a fine family!" "I

17
00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:44.704
owe it all to you!" Jimmy and Mr. Pendleton said to Pollyanna at the same time. They

18
00:01:44.705 --> 00:01:47.905
looked at each other and laughed. Noticing

19
00:01:47.906 --> 00:01:56.643
how happy they were together, Pollyanna smiled. "I'm so glad!" ***

20
00:01:56.644 --> 00:02:03.989
As spring arrived, there was little change in Pollyanna's condition.

21
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:09.673
The townspeople kept up with the latest news, but everyone felt discouraged.

22
00:02:09.674 --> 00:02:15.156
Despite Dr. Mead's treatments, Pollyanna was not improving.

23
00:02:15.157 --> 00:02:18.443
Dr. Chilton was especially concerned about her.

24
00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:26.234
Although he never spoke to Aunt Polly, he always managed to hear about Pollyanna's condition.

25
00:02:26.235 --> 00:02:32.377
"I need to do more than worry about Pollyanna," he thought one day in his office.

26
00:02:32.378 --> 00:02:37.086
The next Saturday morning, he went to see Mr. Pendleton.

27
00:02:37.087 --> 00:02:43.385
It was a lovely spring day, and the windows were open as the two men sat in the library.

28
00:02:43.386 --> 00:02:48.390
"I've come to you because you've lived in this town your whole life," Dr. Chilton said.

29
00:02:48.391 --> 00:02:53.618
"Of anyone here, you know the most about my past relationship with Polly Harrington.

30
00:02:53.619 --> 00:02:58.523
I want to examine Pollyanna. I must examine her!"

31
00:02:58.524 --> 00:03:00.767
"Why can't you?"

32
00:03:00.768 --> 00:03:05.740
"You know very well that I haven't been inside that house for over 15 years.

33
00:03:05.741 --> 00:03:10.174
When Miss Polly and I quarreled, she said she'd never ask me there again.

34
00:03:10.175 --> 00:03:15.128
Not unless she was ready to beg my forgiveness and marry me."

35
00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:18.103
Mr. Pendleton thought for a moment.

36
00:03:18.104 --> 00:03:23.589
"I don't understand why you have to be asked to the house. Can't you go on your own?"

37
00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:32.655
Dr. Chilton shook his head. "Out of courtesy to Dr. Warren and Dr. Mead, I can't just barge in."

38
00:03:32.656 --> 00:03:38.754
"Maybe you need to focus on making up with Miss Polly. What did you quarrel about?"

39
00:03:38.755 --> 00:03:44.829
"Forget the quarrel." The doctor made an impatient gesture and stood up.

40
00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.433
"It was a silly argument about nothing.

41
00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:53.925
What's important is that if I can see Pollyanna, there's a 90 percent chance she'll walk again."

42
00:03:53.926 --> 00:03:59.790
As Dr. Chilton said that in a loud voice, he paced over to the window.

43
00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:03.797
In the garden below, Jimmy was pulling weeds.

44
00:04:03.798 --> 00:04:08.611
He stopped weeding and sat up, his ears wide open. "Pollyanna!

45
00:04:08.612 --> 00:04:14.924
Walk again!" Mr. Pendleton exclaimed. "What are you talking about?" "I

46
00:04:14.925 --> 00:04:19.309
have a doctor friend who specializes in this type of paralysis. From

47
00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:25.857
what I've been able to gather, Pollyanna's case sounds similar to one he just cured." "You

48
00:04:25.858 --> 00:04:30.828
must see her right away!" Mr. Pendleton was now standing too. "Couldn't

49
00:04:30.829 --> 00:04:33.739
you see her through Dr. Warren?" "No!"

50
00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:38.883
Dr. Chilton slammed his fist on Mr. Pendleton's desk. "Dr.

51
00:04:38.884 --> 00:04:42.180
Warren suggested early on that I examine Pollyanna. But

52
00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:47.572
Miss Polly said no so firmly that Dr. Warren didn't dare mention it again." "Miss

53
00:04:47.573 --> 00:04:50.328
Polly must be made to ask you!" "But

54
00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:54.733
how? She's too proud and angry to ask me herself." "Miss

55
00:04:54.734 --> 00:05:01.399
Polly must be made to understand how vitally important this is," Mr. Pendleton said. "And

56
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:07.091
who's going to do that?" Dr. Chilton said bitterly. Mr.

57
00:05:07.092 --> 00:05:12.450
Pendleton groaned. "I have no idea." Outside

58
00:05:12.451 --> 00:05:17.333
the window Jimmy had hardly moved since he started eavesdropping. "I

59
00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:22.518
know," he whispered. " I'm going to do it!"

60
00:05:22.519 --> 00:05:30.905
As fast as he could, Jimmy ran down Pendleton Hill toward Miss Polly's house.

